{
  "id": 983,
  "description": "When kingdoms fall, they do not crumble quietly — they rot from within. And from that rot… rises Blightreign.\n\nBlightreign is not merely a name whispered in fear — it is an era, a curse, a dominion born from decay itself. Where once stood shining citadels and proud banners, now stretch blackened forests and skies choked with ash. Rivers run thick with corruption. The earth trembles beneath unseen horrors. And at the heart of it all stands the sovereign of ruin — a force that does not conquer through fire alone, but through withering inevitability.\n\nIn the age of Blightreign, hope is not extinguished in a single blaze — it is slowly strangled. Crops fail. Armies fracture. Trust erodes. Every victory tastes of poison. Every alliance carries rot beneath its gold.\n\nLegends speak of a throne carved from petrified roots and bone — a throne that feeds on despair. They say the Blightreign does not seek domination for glory… but transformation. A world reshaped in its image: savage, relentless, eternal.\n\nThis is not a storm that passes.\n\nThis is the season of ruin.\n\nThis is Blightreign.",
